speechtext:
I am not backing up;
don't think I am. I know that a little smear campaign went on. I picked up the People's Weekly the other day. My C.C.F. friends may think I do not read the People's Weekly, but I like to read the funny papers occasionally and so I read that, and here on one page I saw in big type: Hansel! scorns his constituents -or something to that effect. I can go before my constituents any time of the year and I am not afraid to put all my cards on the table. The fact of the matter is that what
I said I repeat now, that many of the organizations which sent in those resolutions asking that C.B.C. maintain its present status do not know all the intricacies of radio and do not know the tremendous implications involved in Canada's radio policy.
